`central_measure(values)` accepts a list of finite real numbers excluding booleans. It returns the central sorted value for odd-length input and the arithmetic mean of the two central sorted values for even-length input. An empty list raises `ValueError`. A non-list or non-real element raises `TypeError`; a non-finite element raises `ValueError`. The input list and its elements must not be mutated or reordered.

